-- title:
--   Cusp zero-chart specialisation dictionary under a small opposite coordinate
-- statement:
--   Fix a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a prime $\ell$, a nonzero level $N$ with $N$ squarefree and $\ell \nmid N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$ and a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$. Further data: `data`, a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(\ell)$ killing the pair $(j, j_\ell)$ of $q$-expansions, satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^\ell - Y)(X - Y^\ell) \bmod \ell$; integrality of the two Hecke comparison maps $\overline{\alpha}, \overline{\beta}$ from the base-changed level-$N$ function field into level $N\ell$; a family `dataAll` of such modular polynomial data for every divisor of $N$, with the level-$N$ member symmetric in its two Laurent-series arguments and separable after reduction to $k$ and passage to $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k$; a fibre model `fm` for $N$, $A$, $\ell$, $k$, $\mathrm{red}$ (subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the base-changed function field, integral over the affine bases generated by $A$-constants together with $\bar{j}$ respectively $\bar{j}^{-1}$, equipped with reduction maps $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}, \pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ to the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field $k(j_k, j_{N,k})$); and a cusp chart `cc` for `fm`, asserting that $\bar{j}_N \bar{j}^{-N}$ lies in $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ and reduces to $j_{N,k} j_k^{-N}$. Then for every place $w$ of the level-$N$ base-changed modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $\tau \in A$ such that $t := \bar{j}/\bar{j}_N^{\,N}$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$: if $\mathrm{ord}_w(\bar{j}_N - a) \le 0$ for every $a \in A$, if the residue of $t$ at $w$ is the image of $\tau$ in the residue field of $w$, and if $\bar{j}_N/\bar{j}^{\,N} - a$ is a nonunit of the valuation subring of $w$ for some $a$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, then either $j_k/j_{N,k}^{\,N} - \mathrm{red}(\tau) = 0$, or this element has strictly positive order at the place $\mathrm{spPlace}(w)$ of $k(j_k, j_{N,k})$ attached to `fm`.
--
--   This is one configuration of the specialisation dictionary at the cusps: it transports the statement that the cusp coordinate $t = \bar{j}/\bar{j}_N^{\,N}$ has residue $\tau$ at a characteristic-zero place $w$ to the vanishing, or positive order, of the reduced coordinate at the specialised place in characteristic $\ell$, in the regime where the opposite coordinate $\bar{j}_N/\bar{j}^{\,N}$ is small. It feeds the assembled zero-chart dictionary [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d7_dictZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.spPlace_d7_dictZero).
